# MadGraph process setup for the reference dataset's two-prong signal: a narrow spin-2
# Bulk Graviton decaying to two Higgs-like bosons of variable mass.
#
# Taken from the reference production's own cards, public at
#   colizz/hww-tagging @ dev-miniaods
#   event_producer/cmsconnect_miniaods_scouting_Run3/inputs/InputCards/
#       BulkGravitonToHH_{proc,run,customizecards}_card_instMG.dat
# which that production feeds to MadGraph through its `instMG://` mechanism - a patched
# CMSSW that builds a gridpack per mass point inside the GEN step. We do NOT need any
# of that: this repository already runs MadGraph standalone and hands the LHE to Pythia
# and then to CMSSW (the "hepmc" route, see run.sh), which is what the gridpack
# machinery was working around. The physics is the cards, and those are reproduced here.
#
# The model ships with this process in model/RS_bulk_ktilda (from the public
# dibosonResonanceModel.tar.gz in the same repository). It is a PYTHON-2 era UFO, so it
# must be converted before import - MG5 3.x cannot read it directly. The reference's own
# proc card does the same `convert model` step.
set group_subprocesses Auto
set ignore_six_quark_processes False
set gauge unitary
set complex_mass_scheme False
set auto_update 0
convert model ./model/RS_bulk_ktilda
import model ./model/RS_bulk_ktilda
define p = g u c d s u~ c~ d~ s~
generate p p > y, ( y > H H )
output proc -nojpeg
